# item52 route, item56b form: Hual01a story route, walked. Replaces no prior fixture (first
# route on this map).
#
# Both MapInfo objectives complete through the game's own chains and the level requests the
# campaign travel to Hual01b (NextMapLevelWithUnr), exactly as decoded:
#   - objective 1 "Re-connect the power supply": the EDF-panel handle `Porte6`
#     (XIDCine.Porte, bEaseInteract, Event 'Goal_Manette_EDF') is used in the camp's
#     south-east corner; `TriggerEvent('Goal_Manette_EDF')` reaches XIIIGoalTrigger3
#     (GoalNumber 666) and `XIIIGoalTrigger.CauseGoal` calls MapInfo.SetGoalComplete(666);
#     the map's own override `xidmaps.Hual01a.SetGoalComplete` decodes to: case 666 sets
#     `bYaDuJus = true` (the power is connected), promotes `Objectif[1].bPrimary = true` and
#     calls `SetGoalComplete(1)` - so objective 1 is promoted and completed by game code.
#   - the dam bridge lever `XIIIMover6` (XIDMaps.Hual01a's `BridgeLever`, static mesh
#     statichual01.manette in the crest cabanon, InitialState 'PlayerTriggerToggle', Event
#     'Goal_Manette_Pont', bEaseInteract): the player aims at it and presses use;
#     `XIIIMover.PlayerTriggerToggle.PlayerTrigger` swings the handle (`Open` label,
#     Mover defaults DelayTime 0 / MoveTime 1) and `XIIIMover.FinishedOpening` fires
#     `TriggerEvent('Goal_Manette_Pont')` -> XIIIGoalTrigger2 (GoalNumber 555) ->
#     `CauseGoal` -> `SetGoalComplete(555)`. Case 555 with `bYaDuJus` set checks
#     `TGSDummy == 546` and calls `TriggerEvent('PontA')` (CloseBridgeEvent default):
#     XIIIMover0/5 (Tag 'PontA', MoveTime 4 s) slide the crest panels closed through the
#     game's own mover code, and `CWndFocusTrigger3` (whose `WaitForBeingSeen.Timer` set
#     `self.Tag = self.EventFinFocus` = 'PontA' when the comic-strip window started) runs
#     its own `WaitEndFocus.Trigger` dismissal (RemoveMe + array compaction + Destroy) -
#     the focus window ends through the authored chain, with no input bridge at all. The
#     lever then locks itself (`GotoState('Locked')`, `bNoInteractionIcon = true`).
#     `TGSDummy` is the retail licence-layer flag: nothing in any package writes it; the
#     full game's `AMapInfo::PostBeginPlay` native (Xiii.dll 0x11b01640, measured) writes
#     it from a hard-coded per-map table keyed by `iLoadSpecificValue` (Hual01a: 26 ->
#     546; the demo build leaves 0, which produces the "BUY THE GAME" branch). The port
#     reproduces that native write after the script `PostBeginPlay` (xiii-script VM,
#     licence table, synthetic + corpus tests); the lever use is a real player input and
#     everything downstream is game code.
#   - objective 0 "Penetrate the base enclosure": the end trigger `Trigger2`
#     (Engine.Trigger, Event 'End_of_level') sits inside the sealed dam-base shaft
#     (8426,-6708,-491); touching it fires XIIIGoalTrigger1 (GoalNumber 0, primary) ->
#     CauseGoal -> SetGoalComplete(0) -> TestGoalComplete (both objectives completed) ->
#     DoTravel -> EndGame("GoalComplete") -> GameEndedSuccess -> ServerTravel.
#
# The three labelled teleports cover measured movement gaps of the route driver (all verified
# with xiii-tool box-probe):
#   - t=160: walking west out of the lever cabanon wedges the box on the room's interior
#     partition and the swung-open door leaf (route-v6/v8/v9 logs); the entry walk is unaided.
#   - t=168: item53b combat adaptation (measured). With the corrected mover line-check rule
#     (a registered mover without `bUseCylinderCollision` answers from its mesh, not the
#     Engine.Mover class-default r=160 cylinder) the camp guards' fire connects along the
#     dam-bridge crossing where the phantom cylinders used to absorb it: the 35-health
#     player took hits from t=162 and died at t=178.5 pre-adaptation (hual-skiptrace log).
#     The teleport jumps from the bridge west abutment (4560,-5030) to TouchTrigger6
#     ('dernierephrase', r=350 at (6133.7,-4948.9,-105)) so the bridge-crossing touch still
#     fires on landing, and the east-platform walk resumes from there.
#   - t=187: the dam-base shaft is sealed at every horizontal approach at trigger height
#     (cliff faces y=-6512/-6520 and y=-6920/-6928, the GR_passage tube walls); retail descends
#     it from the cache gallery above. The teleport places the player inside the shaft top so
#     the fall delivers the game's own `Trigger2` touch; the player lands on the tube floor
#     at z=-925 (measured, health intact).
#
# No take_control, no set_goal, no weapon grant (the fresh-login inventory from Hual01a's
# InitialInv/AcceptInventory - Fists, Beretta, FusilPompe, arbalete, LockPick, Hook,
# StunningSkill - is untouched; no objective needs a weapon).
t=0.50 forward 1
t=1.50 forward 0
